WEBVTT

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:22.122
Though you are so close,
Kore hodo soba ni

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:26.626
I cannot tell you how I feel.
Iru no ni tsutaerarezu

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:30.697
The more strongly I feel,
Tsuyoku omou hodo

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:35.301
the harder it is for me to find the words.
Kotoba ga mitsukaranai

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:43.343
What is sad is not fate...
Kanashii no wa unmei ja nakute

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:54.117
...but that all encounters come to an end.
Deai no subete ni owari ga aru koto

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:58.558
O incomplete beings,
Mikan naru mono

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:02.996
awaken, for beyond the night...
mezameyo yoru o koetara

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:07.067
At the end of the desert...
Sabaku no hate ni

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:14.735
...the truth surely awaits you.
Shinjitsu ga matteru yo kitto

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:36.361
Honoka has come to Emporium.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:41.496
With Millie in tow, she went to see
Esmel, Zankan's younger sister.

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:47.205
Esmel was kindhearted, much like Zankan.

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:52.145
For burying Zankan and looking after Millie,

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:53.544
she thanked Honoka over and over again.

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:58.952
Without any prompting,
Esmel said that she would take in Millie...

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:00.749
...and raise her with all due responsibility.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:04.549
She had received word from Honoka in advance.

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:08.826
It seems her heart had been
set upon it since that time.

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:13.233
Millie voiced no complaints as
they made these arrangements...

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:15.167
...and quietly went along with their decision.

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:19.038
It would have been a lie to
say she felt no misgivings.

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:22.405
But she had no choice but to have faith in Millie.

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:26.736
Several days have passed...

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:30.116
I'm stuffed!

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:32.452
Here, look! It's sticking out so much!

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:35.488
That's impressive. What's gotten into you today?

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:38.252
Well, it's tomorrow, right?
That Hono's coming over?!

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:44.719
Yes. She said she would come
see you before a job, didn't she?

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:48.230
I can't wait for it to be tomorrow!

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:01.702
Honoka had left on a journey once again.

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:06.750
Until Dawn

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:18.059
Let's go...

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:20.830
Let's go!

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:22.900
Honoka.

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:24.901
Honoka.

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:26.963
Honoka!

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:39.984
Did I just say something now?

00:03:45.625 --> 00:03:47.889
I had a kind of weird dream.

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:50.224
A dream? About what?

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:52.059
Let's see...

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:53.493
Huh?

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.397
It seems you're still half asleep.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:56.559
Shut up!

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:59.797
Wait, look at how early it is!

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:01.198
Where's Iks?

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:03.206
It seems you really are half asleep.

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:03.774
Huh?

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:07.702
Didn't we drop off Iks in the last town?

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:08.877
Oh...

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:11.050
Right, right.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:12.719
"He has some business to attend to,"

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:15.588
"so we'll part ways for now.
He'll contact us again later."

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:19.251
As I recall, it was you that
reported this back to me.

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:22.224
Right you are.

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:24.931
I believe you did not even confirm
where your client was going,

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:29.698
nor did you arrange where and
how we would be meeting up again.

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:31.263
Are you trying to be snide?

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:35.004
It seems you're awake enough
to pick up on that, at least.

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:37.844
I-It'll be fine.

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:39.539
There's no need to worry about Iks.

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:42.580
He'll pop up out of nowhere again like always.

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:44.444
How can you say that?

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:46.007
How?

00:04:48.688 --> 00:04:52.351
I don't know, but I just have
this feeling that he will.

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:54.422
So, what's up, anyway?

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:57.196
I'm thinking of moving away from this location.

00:04:57.196 --> 00:04:58.629
Huh? Why?

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.764
Armored ants?

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:11.978
It leapt on to our tank about 10 minutes ago.

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:15.311
It's got guts, picking a fight with a tank.

00:05:15.448 --> 00:05:17.939
There's only one that's attached to us.

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:20.711
The rest are sitting tight
in the surrounding area.

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:22.147
Looks like it.

00:05:22.422 --> 00:05:24.891
Also, it isn't clear what the cause is,

00:05:24.891 --> 00:05:28.486
but the one perched on the tank has
an unusually high body temperature.

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:31.631
So, we're going to move?

00:05:31.631 --> 00:05:35.301
We can likely shake it off with the
acceleration from combat deployment.

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:38.702
After that, we can run in silent mode
and find another camping site.

00:05:39.906 --> 00:05:41.874
I suppose so...

00:05:42.108 --> 00:05:43.276
No objections, I trust?

00:05:43.276 --> 00:05:43.935
Then...

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:44.941
Hold on a sec.

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:48.010
What are you planning on doing?

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:51.977
It just kind of bothers me.
I'm gonna go check outside.

00:05:58.424 --> 00:06:00.892
Quite the impressive specimen we've got here.

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:13.666
Armored ants.

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:16.400
Commonly known as "desert mercenaries".

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:20.902
A carnivorous animal that can grow
up to 3 meters from head to tail.

00:06:21.748 --> 00:06:25.548
It is a creature that ranks high in
the food chain on the frontier,

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:29.879
and they always operate in groups of three.

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:32.489
This could be troublesome.

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:42.391
How did things look?

00:06:43.469 --> 00:06:45.061
We might be in a bit of a fix.

00:06:46.038 --> 00:06:48.165
The one on top of the tank...

00:06:49.008 --> 00:06:50.168
It's got wings.

00:06:51.477 --> 00:06:53.104
"Swarming", is it?

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:55.912
Probably.

00:06:56.916 --> 00:07:00.249
Sightings of armored ants with wings is not rare.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:04.519
The individual with wings
is apparently a queen ant.

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:07.660
It is said that they are virtually the same...

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:09.787
...as any other ant found in the desert.

00:07:10.329 --> 00:07:15.460
In other words, all ants have the
potential to become a queen.

00:07:16.836 --> 00:07:19.906
An ant that has become a
queen will leave its old hive...

00:07:19.906 --> 00:07:22.008
...and establish a nest in a separate location.

00:07:22.008 --> 00:07:24.738
That is what is called "swarming".

00:07:26.312 --> 00:07:30.082
It is unknown under what conditions
an ant manifests itself as a queen,

00:07:30.082 --> 00:07:33.245
nor what becomes of the other two ants.

00:07:34.287 --> 00:07:36.482
What Honoka had encountered this night...

00:07:36.889 --> 00:07:40.017
...was a part of that unknown lifecycle.

00:07:42.195 --> 00:07:43.924
What are you thinking?

00:07:43.996 --> 00:07:46.965
Well, just trying to think what to do.

00:07:47.166 --> 00:07:49.035
I see no need for indecision.

00:07:49.035 --> 00:07:51.833
Shaking off one ant is a simple thing.

00:07:51.971 --> 00:07:53.666
I'm sure that's true, but...

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:55.905
It bothers you?

00:07:59.045 --> 00:08:01.411
Her wings have only just grown in.

00:08:01.814 --> 00:08:04.647
I think she might be waiting
until she's able to fly.

00:08:04.951 --> 00:08:07.086
That's not a matter for us
to be concerned about.

00:08:07.086 --> 00:08:08.280
But still...

00:08:08.554 --> 00:08:10.385
It's probably a crucial time for her.

00:08:10.623 --> 00:08:12.818
Maybe that's why she's latched on.

00:08:12.925 --> 00:08:15.120
Thinking that she'd be safe here.

00:08:15.528 --> 00:08:17.330
I understand what you're trying to say,

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:19.457
but I can't say you're being practical.

00:08:20.466 --> 00:08:22.301
We have a job.

00:08:22.301 --> 00:08:25.464
We must arrive in Emporium by tomorrow.

00:08:25.671 --> 00:08:27.104
That's true, but...

00:08:27.673 --> 00:08:30.335
Additionally, weren't you going to go see Millie?

00:08:31.577 --> 00:08:34.847
If we arrive late, you won't
have time to do that, either.

00:08:34.847 --> 00:08:36.075
I know that.

00:08:36.349 --> 00:08:39.886
Walken also said that we should
not interfere with nature...

00:08:39.886 --> 00:08:41.187
...because of a moment of
sentimentality or sympathy...

00:08:41.187 --> 00:08:41.487
I know that!
...because of a moment of
sentimentality or sympathy...

00:08:41.487 --> 00:08:42.249
I know that!

00:08:46.893 --> 00:08:47.791
Sorry.

00:08:50.530 --> 00:08:54.990
It's not as if we know that shaking
off the ant will put it in danger.

00:08:55.234 --> 00:08:57.862
If its wings have already formed...

00:08:58.437 --> 00:08:59.369
Until dawn...

00:09:00.907 --> 00:09:03.467
Let's at least wait until dawn for her.

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:05.507
Until dawn...

00:09:05.912 --> 00:09:08.581
Honoka had blurted it out without meaning to.

00:09:08.581 --> 00:09:12.381
She did not even know herself
why she had said that.

00:09:12.652 --> 00:09:17.112
But from the bottom of her heart, she
felt that was what she wanted to do.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:20.115
Do you have some basis for saying that?

00:09:20.192 --> 00:09:21.181
No...

00:09:21.294 --> 00:09:21.988
But...

00:09:23.329 --> 00:09:24.523
Please.

00:09:25.264 --> 00:09:26.561
Until dawn.

00:09:30.536 --> 00:09:33.198
If that will make you feel better...

00:09:37.443 --> 00:09:40.071
Thank you, Bogie.

00:09:45.418 --> 00:09:47.682
Did something happen
between you and Walken?

00:09:47.987 --> 00:09:49.322
Don't follow me.

00:09:49.322 --> 00:09:50.656
I can't do that.

00:09:50.656 --> 00:09:53.750
Accompanying and protecting you is my job.

00:09:54.026 --> 00:09:57.052
Without permission from Walken,
I can't leave you...

00:09:57.129 --> 00:09:59.461
Shut up! I said, don't follow me, Bogie!

00:10:08.574 --> 00:10:09.563
Just now...

00:10:09.842 --> 00:10:10.467
Honoka.

00:10:11.844 --> 00:10:12.778
What is it?

00:10:12.778 --> 00:10:14.575
Motion signatures approaching.

00:10:14.981 --> 00:10:17.973
Northwest. Most likely
another unit of armored ants.

00:10:18.317 --> 00:10:19.750
A coincidence?

00:10:19.885 --> 00:10:20.442
But...

00:10:20.987 --> 00:10:23.854
Armored ants are very territorial.

00:10:23.956 --> 00:10:27.517
Units coming face to face is something
that should never just happen.

00:10:27.927 --> 00:10:28.621
Yeah, right?

00:10:28.995 --> 00:10:30.796
This is just conjecture,

00:10:30.796 --> 00:10:32.665
but perhaps a newly developed queen ant...

00:10:32.665 --> 00:10:35.896
...becomes an enemy that must
be eliminated by its old hive.

00:10:36.569 --> 00:10:38.799
Then, they're coming after the ant here?

00:10:40.106 --> 00:10:42.040
The two near us are moving.

00:10:42.308 --> 00:10:45.072
Guards? Protecting the queen?

00:10:45.378 --> 00:10:50.049
One of the unit becomes a queen and
the other two become her guards...

00:10:50.049 --> 00:10:51.846
That's not inconceivable.

00:10:52.985 --> 00:10:54.577
They're making contact.

00:10:55.021 --> 00:10:56.079
Pick up the audio!

00:11:15.875 --> 00:11:17.069
It's over.

00:11:31.524 --> 00:11:33.048
Father...

00:12:38.457 --> 00:12:39.424
Honoka.

00:12:39.825 --> 00:12:40.655
Honoka!

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:43.529
Motion signatures. Three of them.

00:12:43.529 --> 00:12:45.190
Another unit's approaching.

00:12:46.198 --> 00:12:48.564
We can't do this anymore. Get back inside.

00:12:48.667 --> 00:12:49.827
We'll go into combat deployment.

00:12:51.103 --> 00:12:52.538
You want to fly, don't you?

00:12:52.538 --> 00:12:53.505
Honoka!

00:12:53.739 --> 00:12:54.740
Until dawn...

00:12:54.740 --> 00:12:56.208
What are you saying?

00:12:56.208 --> 00:12:57.835
Another unit is almost on top of us.

00:12:59.512 --> 00:13:01.747
You could kill them out there.

00:13:01.747 --> 00:13:04.443
But another unit will just show up again.

00:13:04.817 --> 00:13:06.842
This is a problem among the ants.

00:13:07.286 --> 00:13:11.257
Or will you take out dozens of
other ants just to protect one...

00:13:11.257 --> 00:13:12.324
Just this once.

00:13:12.324 --> 00:13:12.949
What?

00:13:13.058 --> 00:13:14.457
It'll be just this once.

00:13:46.625 --> 00:13:48.561
You put them in a state of suspended animation?

00:13:48.561 --> 00:13:50.756
I wasn't sure if I could do it or not, but...

00:13:51.096 --> 00:13:52.791
It's Walken's technique, isn't it?

00:13:52.865 --> 00:13:57.136
If I hold them off like this,
no other unit will approach us.

00:13:57.136 --> 00:14:00.072
I should only have to deal with these three.

00:14:00.072 --> 00:14:02.006
In theory, but...

00:14:02.174 --> 00:14:03.943
How much longer until the sun rises?

00:14:03.943 --> 00:14:06.579
In this season, just under two hours, but...

00:14:06.579 --> 00:14:08.513
You plan to keep that up for two hours?

00:14:09.048 --> 00:14:10.482
Let me do this, Bogie.

00:14:10.482 --> 00:14:13.252
Why? Why are you so hung up about this?

00:14:13.252 --> 00:14:15.187
Normally, you would be a little more rational...

00:14:15.187 --> 00:14:16.381
I don't know.

00:14:16.822 --> 00:14:18.915
I don't know myself, either.

00:14:18.991 --> 00:14:19.855
But...

00:14:20.192 --> 00:14:22.962
But see, I want to let her fly.

00:14:22.962 --> 00:14:24.623
I want to protect her!

00:14:25.364 --> 00:14:26.023
Bogie!

00:14:26.932 --> 00:14:28.923
I was given a task by Walken.

00:14:29.335 --> 00:14:33.237
If you attempt to act recklessly,
my job is to dissuade you.

00:14:33.339 --> 00:14:34.636
That's true, but...

00:14:34.874 --> 00:14:37.176
But we have a long history between us.

00:14:37.176 --> 00:14:39.076
I know you well.

00:14:39.144 --> 00:14:41.305
In a way, even better than Walken.

00:14:42.381 --> 00:14:43.075
Bogie!

00:14:43.415 --> 00:14:44.884
Just this once.

00:14:44.884 --> 00:14:47.944
If nothing changes by dawn,
we leave this place.

00:14:48.153 --> 00:14:51.452
Just as if I had determined
that you were in danger.

00:14:51.724 --> 00:14:55.751
If you say you are unwilling to let go,
I will kill this ant myself.

00:14:56.061 --> 00:14:57.255
Those are the conditions.

00:14:57.696 --> 00:14:58.754
Okay!

00:15:03.402 --> 00:15:05.495
Please, save it!

00:15:30.062 --> 00:15:32.929
Don't worry. I only put it into a
state of suspended animation.

00:15:34.099 --> 00:15:35.601
Rather than cutting your opponent,

00:15:35.601 --> 00:15:38.070
you slam them with your "cutting" energy...

00:15:38.070 --> 00:15:40.664
...and make your opponent
believe that you cut them.

00:15:41.273 --> 00:15:43.104
This is another way of fighting.

00:15:44.376 --> 00:15:46.278
People should not act on momentary emotions...

00:15:46.278 --> 00:15:48.547
...and interfere with the workings of nature.

00:15:48.547 --> 00:15:51.050
Life and death. Those that eat and are eaten.

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:53.280
All things exist alike.

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:56.010
This time was special.

00:15:56.488 --> 00:15:59.325
After this, no matter how you beg,
I will not save it again.

00:15:59.325 --> 00:16:00.155
Do you understand?

00:16:07.333 --> 00:16:11.337
Even if that sun slips down...

00:16:11.337 --> 00:16:15.975
...into the eastern sky,

00:16:15.975 --> 00:16:24.516
my hidden vow cannot be tarnished.

00:16:24.516 --> 00:16:32.558
When you have someone in your heart to protect,

00:16:32.558 --> 00:16:35.494
only then does anyone become truly strong.

00:16:35.494 --> 00:16:37.363
Drawing your sword and swinging it.
Only then does anyone become truly strong.

00:16:37.363 --> 00:16:37.596
Only then does anyone become truly strong.

00:16:37.596 --> 00:16:40.265
Honoka, that comes easily to you.
Only then does anyone become truly strong.

00:16:40.265 --> 00:16:40.399
Only then does anyone become truly strong.

00:16:40.399 --> 00:16:43.425
So there are other things you must learn.
Only then does anyone become truly strong.

00:16:43.535 --> 00:16:43.769
There are other things?

00:16:43.769 --> 00:16:45.170
There are other things?
If so, I will fight...

00:16:45.170 --> 00:16:46.572
Things about life.
If so, I will fight...

00:16:46.572 --> 00:16:47.272
If so, I will fight...

00:16:47.272 --> 00:16:47.873
A sword is only a tool.
If so, I will fight...

00:16:47.873 --> 00:16:49.341
A sword is only a tool.
...for love in my quest for you.

00:16:49.341 --> 00:16:52.411
...for love in my quest for you.

00:16:52.411 --> 00:16:52.478
With my love for you,

00:16:52.478 --> 00:16:54.646
There will come a time when you, too,
will depart on a journey.
With my love for you,

00:16:54.646 --> 00:16:56.515
When that time comes,
your sword will show you...
With my love for you,

00:16:56.515 --> 00:16:58.250
When that time comes,
your sword will show you...
there is no freedom I cannot relinquish.

00:16:58.250 --> 00:17:00.419
...the path your life should follow.
There is no freedom I cannot relinquish.

00:17:00.419 --> 00:17:03.582
There is no freedom I cannot relinquish.

00:17:59.478 --> 00:18:00.679
Are you all right?

00:18:00.679 --> 00:18:02.915
How long... has it been?

00:18:02.915 --> 00:18:04.712
It'll be two hours soon.

00:18:17.830 --> 00:18:19.320
It's becoming less effective.

00:18:19.565 --> 00:18:21.157
The intervals are growing shorter.

00:18:27.473 --> 00:18:28.201
Damn!

00:18:41.487 --> 00:18:42.852
Get back in! You can't hold them off anymore!

00:18:43.755 --> 00:18:46.125
It's not like you to be so panicked.

00:18:46.125 --> 00:18:46.825
Honoka!

00:18:46.825 --> 00:18:47.587
We made a promise.

00:18:49.328 --> 00:18:50.317
Honoka!

00:19:05.277 --> 00:19:06.972
She flew! She flew!

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:09.274
Honoka!

00:20:02.668 --> 00:20:03.657
Let's go...

00:20:05.404 --> 00:20:06.302
Let's go!

00:20:09.675 --> 00:20:13.941
Honoka was remembering a dawn
that she saw in her dreams.

00:20:14.513 --> 00:20:17.846
The dawn of the morning she had
decided to leave on her journey.

00:20:18.784 --> 00:20:21.053
Maybe it was because she saw
that dawn in her dream...

00:20:21.053 --> 00:20:24.750
...that she had wanted to protect the queen ant.

00:20:25.023 --> 00:20:28.424
Perhaps she saw herself in that queen ant.

00:20:29.294 --> 00:20:33.890
Or was that the queen ant's dream?

00:20:34.299 --> 00:20:37.097
Her hopes and fears of the future...

00:20:37.202 --> 00:20:40.372
Perhaps they resonated with
Honoka's own emotions...

00:20:40.372 --> 00:20:42.932
...and made her see that dream.

00:20:44.042 --> 00:20:46.311
There was no knowing the truth of it,

00:20:46.311 --> 00:20:49.007
but Honoka thought that was all right.

00:20:49.514 --> 00:20:51.505
She had no regrets.

00:20:51.883 --> 00:20:55.621
If she had any, it was that she had
caused her partner to worry.

00:20:55.621 --> 00:20:57.248
That was all.

00:20:57.623 --> 00:20:58.920
Satisfied?

00:20:58.991 --> 00:21:00.083
I suppose.

00:21:01.026 --> 00:21:01.515
Bogie?

00:21:04.096 --> 00:21:05.120
Thank you.

00:21:08.367 --> 00:21:09.732
Wow!

00:21:15.907 --> 00:21:18.603
Oh? Millie, awake already?

00:21:19.211 --> 00:21:20.610
Morning, Auntie.

00:21:22.414 --> 00:21:23.346
Morning.

00:21:26.952 --> 00:21:29.614
Dawn comes to us all.

00:21:30.656 --> 00:21:34.717
The time to leave on a journey
comes to us all as well.

00:21:37.729 --> 00:21:38.923
Good luck.

00:21:45.070 --> 00:21:48.006
A flexible civilization...
Juunan na bunmei wa

00:21:48.006 --> 00:21:50.509
...is always rapidly advancing.
Itsudatte nisshin-geppo

00:21:50.509 --> 00:21:53.478
You and your dreams are also...
Kimi to yume mo

00:21:53.478 --> 00:21:57.278
...making headway even now.
Genzai shinkou

00:22:02.788 --> 00:22:05.757
I realized for the first time...
Hajimete kizuitan da

00:22:05.757 --> 00:22:09.454
...with that line, resembling a surprise attack.
Fui-uchi ni nita sono serifu de

00:22:14.499 --> 00:22:17.436
My sixth sense was pried open.
Kojiakerareta dai-rokkan

00:22:17.436 --> 00:22:21.463
I'd been waiting for this feeling this whole time.
Kono kankaku o zutto matteita

00:22:25.477 --> 00:22:28.447
Opening my heart, just opening it...
Kokoro o hiraite tada hiraite

00:22:28.447 --> 00:22:31.416
I embrace the voices of strangers.
Daisansha no koe ukeireru

00:22:31.416 --> 00:22:34.286
Earnestly persevering, just persevering...
Hitasura koraete tada koraete

00:22:34.286 --> 00:22:37.380
I even try turning pages of criticism.
Hinan no peeji mo aketemiru

00:22:37.689 --> 00:22:40.659
I'm going to leave my...
Toushindai no boku wa

00:22:40.659 --> 00:22:43.595
...true-to-life self behind, right here.
Koko ni oite iku yo

00:22:43.595 --> 00:22:47.399
You can say whatever you want now...
Mou nanto itte kuretemo

00:22:47.399 --> 00:22:48.957
...and I'm fine with that.
Kekkou da

00:22:49.468 --> 00:22:54.940
Ah, how simple is the impulse to evolve.
Aa nante tanjun da shinka shitai to iu shoudou

00:22:54.940 --> 00:22:57.843
You and your dreams are also...
Kimi to yume mo

00:22:57.843 --> 00:23:01.040
...making headway even now.
Genzai shinkou

00:23:15.160 --> 00:23:16.889
Preview

00:23:17.095 --> 00:23:19.264
After finishing a job,

00:23:19.264 --> 00:23:22.392
we ran into the unusual situation
of a sand dragon stampede.

00:23:22.567 --> 00:23:24.469
Coming back from our thrilling experience,

00:23:24.469 --> 00:23:26.869
the atmosphere in Emporium soothes us.

00:23:27.205 --> 00:23:29.673
But the respite was short-lived.

00:23:30.075 --> 00:23:32.669
An encounter with the mysterious beauty, Paife,

00:23:32.744 --> 00:23:34.268
and a new job.

00:23:34.479 --> 00:23:37.243
A vaguely ominous atmosphere was drifting in.

00:23:37.616 --> 00:23:40.786
Next time on
The Third - The Girl With The Blue Eye,

00:23:40.786 --> 00:23:42.053
episode 8, "An Afternoon in Emporium".

00:23:42.053 --> 00:23:43.488
An Afternoon in Emporium
episode 8, "An Afternoon in Emporium".

00:23:43.488 --> 00:23:44.921
An Afternoon in Emporium
